## 8. Conversation Context Management -- `ConversationManager.swift`

This is where persistence happens. The conversation history is a rolling window of check-in exchanges.

```swift
final class ConversationManager {
    private let maxHistoryPairs = 10  // Keep last 10 exchanges (20 messages)
    private let storageURL: URL

    private(set) var history: [ClaudeMessage] = []

    init() {
        // Store in ~/Library/Application Support/ClippyMac/
        let appSupport = FileManager.default.urls(for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask).first!
        storageURL = appSupport.appendingPathComponent("ClippyMac/conversation.json")
    }

    func addExchange(userMessage: ClaudeMessage, assistantResponse: String) {
        history.append(userMessage)
        history.append(ClaudeMessage(
            role: "assistant",
            content: [.text(.init(type: "text", text: assistantResponse))]
        ))

        // Trim to max history (keep recent, drop old)
        if history.count > maxHistoryPairs * 2 {
            // Replace old image blocks with text summaries to save tokens
            history = Array(history.suffix(maxHistoryPairs * 2))
        }

        save()
    }

    /// Before sending to API, strip base64 image data from older messages
    /// to keep request size manageable. Replace with "[screenshot]" placeholder.
    func messagesForAPI() -> [ClaudeMessage] {
        return history.enumerated().map { index, message in
            // Only keep image data for the most recent user message
            if index < history.count - 2 && message.role == "user" {
                let strippedContent = message.content.map { block -> ContentBlock in
                    if case .image = block {
                        return .text(.init(type: "text", text: "[previous screenshot]"))
                    }
                    return block
                }
                return ClaudeMessage(role: message.role, content: strippedContent)
            }
            return message
        }
    }

    private func save() { /* JSON encode history to storageURL */ }
    func load() { /* JSON decode history from storageURL */ }
}
```

Critical design decision: **strip base64 image data from older messages before sending to the API**. Each screenshot is ~100-500KB of base64 text. Sending 10 screenshots per request would be 1-5MB of request body and thousands of wasted tokens. Only the current screenshot is sent as an image; older check-ins retain their text context (app name, window title, timestamp) and the assistant's response, but the image is replaced with a `[previous screenshot]` placeholder. This preserves conversational continuity while keeping costs and latency reasonable.

**Persistence location**: `~/Library/Application Support/ClippyMac/conversation.json`. This survives app restarts. On each launch, `load()` restores context. The conversation resets only if the user explicitly clears it or if the file is deleted.

